## Scenarios

### PostgreSQL mimic compiled entry closure

#### parses its own argv flags without the broad CLI or IO utility graph

- Verify: parses its own argv flags without the broad CLI or IO utility graph
   - Expected: help.exit_code equals `0`
- A missing --query is the entrypoint's own terminating diagnostic
   - Expected: noquery.exit_code equals `2)  # oracle: 2 — required-flag error status`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 11 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-POSTGRESMIMI-001
step("Verify: parses its own argv flags without the broad CLI or IO utility graph")
val bin = "/mnt/data/worktrees/simple-main/bin/simple"
val entry = "src/app/postgres_mimic_server/main.spl"
val help = run(bin, ["run", entry, "--help"])
expect(help.exit_code).to_equal(0)
expect(help.stdout).to_contain("Usage: postgres-mimic-server --db <path> --query <sql>")
step("A missing --query is the entrypoint's own terminating diagnostic")
val noquery = run(bin, ["run", entry])
expect(noquery.exit_code).to_equal(2)  # oracle: 2 — required-flag error status
expect(noquery.stdout).to_contain("error: --query is required")
```

</details>

#### keeps the pure-Simple PostgreSQL mimic database capsule

- Verify: keeps the pure-Simple PostgreSQL mimic database capsule
- The query is answered by the mimic capsule in PostgreSQL protocol terms
   - Expected: result.exit_code equals `1)  # oracle: 1 — error responses exit nonzero`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 9 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-POSTGRESMIMI-001
step("Verify: keeps the pure-Simple PostgreSQL mimic database capsule")
val bin = "/mnt/data/worktrees/simple-main/bin/simple"
val entry = "src/app/postgres_mimic_server/main.spl"
val db_path = "/tmp/simple_pg_mimic_spec_" + str(rt_getpid()) + ".pdb"
val result = run(bin, ["run", entry, "--db", db_path, "--query", "select 1"])
step("The query is answered by the mimic capsule in PostgreSQL protocol terms")
expect(result.exit_code).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 — error responses exit nonzero
expect(result.stdout).to_contain("ERROR 42601")
```

</details>

#### answers from its own closure instead of the general CLI facade

- Verify: answers from its own closure instead of the general CLI facade
- The usage text is the mimic's own, not the general CLI bootstrap banner
   - Expected: result.stdout does not contain `bootstrap`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-APP-POSTGRESMIMI-001
step("Verify: answers from its own closure instead of the general CLI facade")
val bin = "/mnt/data/worktrees/simple-main/bin/simple"
val entry = "src/app/postgres_mimic_server/main.spl"
val result = run(bin, ["run", entry, "--help"])
step("The usage text is the mimic's own, not the general CLI bootstrap banner")
expect(result.stdout).to_contain("postgres-mimic-server")
expect(result.stdout.contains("bootstrap")).to_equal(false)
```

</details>

